Feature: slice-5 / flutter-web-target
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-5
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.3 (Flutter Web therapist console)

What was built
==============
- Confirmed `flutter-app/superwizor/web/` already exists from an
  earlier `flutter create --platforms web .` — no need to re-run
  the scaffold.
- `flutter build web --no-tree-shake-icons` (Flutter 3.41.9 stable)
  produces `flutter-app/superwizor/build/web/` (45 MB,
  CanvasKit-rendered). Build clean both before AND after the
  recording-screen guard.
- Recording-screen kIsWeb guard added at
  `flutter-app/superwizor/lib/screens/recording_screen.dart`:
  the build() method short-circuits to a new `_WebRecordingFallback`
  widget on web that explains "Nagrywanie dostępne w aplikacji iOS"
  with the patient alias inlined. docs/18 §8.3 calls this out
  explicitly: "❌ recording_screen.dart — replaced with a friendly
  'Use the iPhone app to record' CTA".
- `flutter analyze` on the changed file: No issues found.

Existing iOS code that needed no changes
========================================
- `lib/screens/login_screen.dart` — renders identically on web
  (verified via the served bundle — see flutter-web-launch.png).
- `lib/screens/menu_screen.dart`, `home_screen.dart`,
  `client_details_screen.dart`, `session_details_screen.dart`,
  `transcript`/`report` screens — none use platform-specific APIs.
  Riverpod, gRPC-Web (already used over CONNECT), Firestore Web
  SDK, all work as-is. (Will be re-verified in features 3-4 when
  we walk the actual flows on web.)
- `firebase_options.dart` already includes the `kIsWeb` branch
  selecting the web platform config.
- The pubspec depends on `record`, `pdfx`, and
  `flutter_secure_storage`, all of which have web platform support.
  Wasm dry-run flags some `dart:html` / `dart:js_util` uses in
  flutter_secure_storage_web + pdfx; non-fatal under CanvasKit/HTML
  renderer.

How verified
============
1. `flutter pub get` ran cleanly (70 packages have newer minor
   versions but constraints not bumped — separate hygiene task).
2. `flutter build web --no-tree-shake-icons` → exit 0,
   "✓ Built build/web". Captured at
   evidence/.../build.log. Both rounds (before and after the
   kIsWeb guard) succeeded.
3. Served the bundle via `python3 -m http.server 8765` and hit it
   with puppeteer at 1280×800 — `flutter-web-launch.png` captures
   the login screen rendering with all Euphire tokens applied:
     • "Superwizor AI." brand heading in Ember
     • "Zaloguj się, aby kontynuować." subtitle in Mist
     • Email + password inputs with Frost/05 glass surface
     • Ember "Zaloguj się." submit
     • "Nie pamiętam hasła." + "Nie masz konta? Zarejestruj się."
       links in Ember
   Polish diacritics (ę, ł, ą, ż) all render correctly.
4. `flutter analyze lib/screens/recording_screen.dart` → No
   issues found.

What's NOT done in this feature (deferred to subsequent Slice 5 features)
=========================================================================
- Full audit of every screen for browser-incompatibility. Features
  3 (therapist console) + 4 (profile edit) walk the actual flows
  and will surface any remaining gaps screen-by-screen.
- New `web/index.html` polish (title, og:meta, manifest icons).
  Current uses the default `flutter create` template. Slice 6
  i18n-polish-launch updates it alongside the marketing site's
  prod assets.
- `kIsWeb` guards on `new_session_screen.dart`'s recording
  branch + the upload-queue's local-file paths. The build doesn't
  break without them today because the code paths are gated by
  user navigation, but feature 3 (therapist-console) will need to
  surface "upload audio" as the only entry path on web.
- Shared-machine warning ("for use on personal devices only") on
  the login footer — Slice 6.
- The auth status badge from the marketing site is irrelevant
  here; the Flutter Web app has its own session state via Firebase
  Auth's IndexedDB persistence.

Compliance with docs/18 §8.3
============================
- ✓ Web platform enabled, `flutter build web` produces the bundle
  Firebase Hosting expects at `flutter-app/superwizor/build/web`
  (matches the `superwizor-app` site config in firebase.json from
  Slice 2 feature 8).
- ✓ recording_screen.dart replaced with the "use the iPhone app"
  CTA on web.
- ☐ new_session_screen.dart's recording branch — deferred to
